description: |
  A post indoors takes any nail. One imperial and one metric: a bright 16d
  common nail driven home, and a hot-dip galvanized 3.4 x 90 mm wire nail - an
  outdoor nail, which goes wherever any nail does - driven 40 mm of the 88.9 mm
  it will go.

  Neither connection names an interface. The nail's point and the post's target
  are found by their mating, and the target's 'drive' says how far in each nail
  is.
links:
  - part: example/post
    name: post

  - part: imperial:common/16d
    name: bright
    connect:
      name: post
      toInstance: A
      toParams: { drive: 88.9 }

  - part: metric:flat/3.4x90
    name: galvanized
    params: { coating: hot-dip-galvanized }
    connect:
      name: post
      toInstance: B
      toParams: { drive: 40 }
